{"game_id":2026020111,"away":"SEA","home":"TBL","split":{"name":"Montour","side":0,"sec":1388},"lede":"Tampa Bay had last change, so Jon Cooper picked most of these matchups. Tampa Bay played without Charle-Édouard D'Astous and Gage Goncalves. Seattle lost Brandon Montour after 3:08 of the second.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"Kucherov’s line drew Beniers’s line","text":"Jon Cooper sent Hagel, Cirelli and Kucherov out for 9:48 of their 11:08 at 5-on-5 against McCann, Beniers and Samoskevich (88%, about 26% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 0.46 to 0.28 expected goals. Seattle scored one of its three goals then."},{"kind":"match","head":"The third line drew Eberle’s line","text":"Mikheyev, Girgensons and Holmberg spent 9:55 of their 11:59 at 5-on-5 against McMann, Stephenson and Eberle (83%, about 27% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 0.24 to 0.08 expected goals."},{"kind":"match","head":"The fourth line drew Gaudreau’s line","text":"Viel, James and Geekie spent 8:11 of their 10:28 at 5-on-5 against Meyers, Gaudreau and Winterton (78%, about 26% with no line matching), and they had the worse of the chances, 0.11 to 0.60 expected goals."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Montour left, the lines changed but the matchups held","text":"Gaudreau went from 22% to 32% of Seattle’s 5-on-5 time. The matchups stayed: Kucherov’s line against Seattle’s third line (67% before, 51% after) and Kucherov’s line against Seattle’s second line (100% before, 82% after)."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went better","text":"Seattle had 1.09 to 1.67 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Montour left and 1.21 to 0.97 after. Seattle trailed for most of that stretch, though, and a team behind usually pushes the play, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Jon Cooper matched harder than in his other home games: each line spent 76% of its time against one opposing line, against 47% to 71% in his first three.","periods":{"all":{"0":{"r